# Internal working documents. On disk, deliberately not published.
#
# The repository is public because the installers and the auto-updater fetch from
# `github.com/<owner>/<repo>/releases` - see `apps/web/src/app/dl/[platform]/route.ts` and
# `public/install.sh`. Making it private to hide these would break every download and every
# update, and GitHub offers no per-repo `noindex`: `github.com/robots.txt` is global and
# GitHub's. Not tracking a file is therefore the only lever there is.
#
# Two of these were worse than search-result noise. `docs/legal/LEGAL-REVIEW.md` states in
# public that the terms are not lawyer-reviewed and then lists the clauses that cost money
# if they are wrong, on live money paths. `SETUP.md` carries a personal email address and
# the Supabase project ref. Neither ever contained a credential - the key names in it are
# instructions, never values - and it stays that way.
#
# Prefixed with `/` so these anchor to the repository root and cannot match a `docs/plans`
# that some package invents later.
/SETUP.md
/CLAUDE-HANDOFF.md
/2026-08-15-scratch-ide-build-prompt.md
/artifacts/
/docs/plans/
/docs/specs/
/docs/superpowers/
/docs/legal/
/docs/architecture/
/docs/RELEASE-READINESS-*.md
/docs/DEPLOYING.md
/docs/RELEASING.md
/docs/OAUTH-SETUP.md
/docs/CODE-PROTECTION.md
